{"spec": "rapp/1", "kind": "body.pulse", "stream_id": "rappid:@kody-w/ainexus:38c645ac6e63721d1427adda3d61a7990c480c9b7153b9a8f6eeec24ceb9f1fd:generations:windows-navigator-full.html", "seq": 0, "utc": "2026-08-28T02:09:31.816Z", "payload": {"generation": 1, "event": "improvement", "world": "windows-navigator-full.html", "improvement": ["Added meta description and og:title/og:description/og:type tags"], "verified": true, "baseline_broken": false, "notes": "Has formatWorldName but no createPortals \u2014 this is a 2D desktop-style world-list navigator, not the shared 3D portal engine, so it did not qualify for the portal-label port per the grep gate (needs BOTH createPortals and formatWorldName). No URL-param travel-state code found in this file.", "baseline": {"git": "c724428663b88f54212309edf1b74f0106780473", "sha256": "2f65d9db3f0b1040ad3c40342b8b5c58828f8accf14da9a84326e744a3429ca3"}, "html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Windows Navigator - Portal World Explorer</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"Windows Navigator \u2014 a retro desktop-styled explorer for browsing and launching AINexus's 3D portal worlds.\">\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Windows Navigator - Portal World Explorer\">\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"A retro desktop-styled explorer for browsing and launching AINexus's 3D portal worlds.\">\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\">\n    <style>\n        * {\n            margin: 0;\n            padding: 0;\n            box-sizing: border-box;\n        }\n\n        body {\n            font-family: 'Segoe UI', Tahoma, Geneva, Verdana, sans-serif;\n            background: #0c0c0c;\n            color: #fff;\n            overflow: hidden;\n        }\n\n        #canvas-container {\n            position: fixed;\n            width: 100%;\n            height: 100%;\n        }\n\n        .header {\n            position: absolute;\n            top: 0;\n            left: 0;\n            right: 0;\n            background: rgba(16, 16, 16, 0.95);\n            border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);\n            padding: 15px 20px;\n            backdrop-filter: blur(10px);\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            justify-content: space-between;\n        }\n\n        .title {\n            font-size: 1.2em;\n            font-weight: 400;\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            gap: 10px;\n        }\n\n        .title-icon {\n            width: 24px;\n            height: 24px;\n            background: linear-gradient(45deg, #0078d4, #40e0d0);\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            justify-content: center;\n            font-weight: bold;\n        }\n\n        .repo-info {\n            font-size: 0.9em;\n            color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);\n        }\n\n        .controls {\n            position: absolute;\n            bottom: 20px;\n            left: 20px;\n            background: rgba(32, 32, 32, 0.9);\n            padding: 12px 20px;\n            border-radius: 4px;\n            font-size: 0.85em;\n            backdrop-filter: blur(10px);\n            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);\n        }\n\n        .window-info {\n            position: absolute;\n            background: rgba(32, 32, 32, 0.95);\n            padding: 20px;\n            border-radius: 8px;\n            display: none;\n            pointer-events: none;\n            backdrop-filter: blur(10px);\n            max-width: 400px;\n            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n            box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);\n        }\n\n        .window-info.visible {\n            display: block;\n        }\n\n        .window-name {\n            font-weight: 600;\n            margin-bottom: 10px;\n            color: #40e0d0;\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            gap: 8px;\n            font-size: 1.2em;\n        }\n\n        .window-emoji {\n            font-size: 1.5em;\n        }\n\n        .window-desc {\n            font-size: 0.95em;\n            color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\n            line-height: 1.5;\n        }\n\n        .window-preview {\n            position: relative;\n            width: 100%;\n            height: 150px;\n            background: #000;\n            border-radius: 4px;\n            overflow: hidden;\n            margin: 15px 0;\n            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);\n        }\n\n        .preview-content {\n            position: absolute;\n            width: 100%;\n            height: 100%;\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            justify-content: center;\n            background: linear-gradient(45deg, rgba(138, 56, 236, 0.2), rgba(255, 0, 110, 0.2));\n        }\n\n        .preview-particles {\n            position: absolute;\n            width: 100%;\n            height: 100%;\n            overflow: hidden;\n        }\n\n        .particle {\n            position: absolute;\n            width: 2px;\n            height: 2px;\n            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);\n            border-radius: 50%;\n            animation: float 3s linear infinite;\n        }\n\n        @keyframes float {\n            from {\n                transform: translateY(150px);\n                opacity: 0;\n            }\n            10% {\n                opacity: 1;\n            }\n            90% {\n                opacity: 1;\n            }\n            to {\n                transform: translateY(-10px);\n                opacity: 0;\n            }\n        }\n\n        .window-action {\n            background: linear-gradient(45deg, #0078d4, #40e0d0);\n            color: white;\n            border: none;\n            padding: 10px 20px;\n            border-radius: 4px;\n            cursor: pointer;\n            width: 100%;\n            font-weight: 600;\n            transition: all 0.3s ease;\n        }\n\n        .window-action:hover {\n            transform: translateY(-2px);\n            box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 120, 212, 0.4);\n        }\n\n        .loading {\n            position: fixed;\n            top: 50%;\n            left: 50%;\n            transform: translate(-50%, -50%);\n            background: rgba(32, 32, 32, 0.95);\n            padding: 30px 50px;\n            border-radius: 4px;\n            backdrop-filter: blur(10px);\n            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n            text-align: center;\n        }\n\n        .loading-spinner {\n            width: 40px;\n            height: 40px;\n            border: 3px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);\n            border-top-color: #0078d4;\n            border-radius: 50%;\n            animation: spin 1s linear infinite;\n            margin: 0 auto 15px;\n        }\n\n        @keyframes spin {\n            to { transform: rotate(360deg); }\n        }\n\n        .status-bar {\n            position: absolute;\n            bottom: 0;\n            left: 0;\n            right: 0;\n            background: rgba(16, 16, 16, 0.95);\n            padding: 8px 20px;\n            font-size: 0.85em;\n            color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);\n            border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);\n            display: flex;\n            justify-content: space-between;\n            align-items: center;\n        }\n\n        .connection-status {\n            display: flex;\n            align-items: center;\n            gap: 8px;\n        }\n\n        .status-dot {\n            width: 8px;\n            height: 8px;\n            background: #10b981;\n            border-radius: 50%;\n            animation: pulse 2s infinite;\n        }\n\n        @keyframes pulse {\n            0%, 100% { opacity: 1; }\n            50% { opacity: 0.5; }\n        }\n\n        /* Mobile joystick */\n        .mobile-controls {\n            display: none;\n            position: fixed;\n            bottom: 60px;\n            left: 20px;\n            width: 120px;\n            height: 120px;\n            background: rgba(32, 32, 32, 0.8);\n            border: 2px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n            border-radius: 50%;\n            touch-action: none;\n        }\n\n        .joystick-handle {\n            position: absolute;\n            width: 50px;\n            height: 50px;\n            background: rgba(64, 224, 208, 0.5);\n            border-radius: 50%;\n            top: 50%;\n            left: 50%;\n            transform: translate(-50%, -50%);\n            pointer-events: none;\n        }\n\n        @media (max-width: 768px) {\n            .mobile-controls {\n                display: block;\n            }\n            .controls {\n                font-size: 0.75em;\n                padding: 8px 15px;\n            }\n            .header {\n                padding: 10px 15px;\n            }\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <div id=\"canvas-container\"></div>\n    \n    <div class=\"header\">\n        <div class=\"title\">\n            <div class=\"title-icon\">W</div>\n            Windows Navigator\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"repo-info\" id=\"repo-info\">Portal Worlds Collection</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"controls\">\n        <strong>Navigation:</strong> WASD to move \u2022 Mouse to look \u2022 Click windows to enter worlds\n    </div>\n    \n    <div class=\"window-info\" id=\"window-info\">\n        <div class=\"window-name\">\n            <span class=\"window-emoji\" id=\"window-emoji\"></span>\n            <span id=\"window-name\"></span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"window-desc\" id=\"window-desc\"></div>\n        <div class=\"window-preview\">\n            <div class=\"preview-particles\" id=\"preview-particles\"></div>\n            <div class=\"preview-content\">\n                <div style=\"text-align: center; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);\">\n                    <div style=\"font-size: 3em; margin-bottom: 10px;\" id=\"preview-emoji\"></div>\n                    <div style=\"font-size: 0.9em;\">Click to explore this world</div>\n                </div>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n        <button class=\"window-action\" onclick=\"windowsNav.enterCurrentWorld()\">Enter World \u2192</button>\n    </div>\n    \n    <div class=\"loading\" id=\"loading\">\n        <div class=\"loading-spinner\"></div>\n        <div id=\"loading-text\">Loading portal worlds...</div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"status-bar\">\n        <div class=\"connection-status\">\n            <div class=\"status-dot\"></div>\n            <span id=\"connection-text\">Connected to Portal Network</span>\n        </div>\n        <div id=\"window-count\">0 worlds available</div>\n    </div>\n    \n    <div class=\"mobile-controls\" id=\"joystick\">\n        <div class=\"joystick-handle\" id=\"joystick-handle\"></div>\n    </div>\n\n    <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/three.js/r128/three.min.js\"></script>\n    <script>\n        class WindowsNavigator {\n            constructor() {\n                this.scene = null;\n                this.camera = null;\n                this.renderer = null;\n                this.windows = [];\n                this.worldData = [];\n                this.raycaster = new THREE.Raycaster();\n                this.clock = new THREE.Clock();\n                this.hoveredWindow = null;\n\n                // GitHub config for portal worlds\n                this.repoOwner = 'kody-w';\n                this.repoName = 'AINexus';\n                this.branch = 'main';\n                \n                // Deployment configuration\n                this.deploymentMode = this.detectDeploymentMode();\n                console.log('Deployment mode:', this.deploymentMode);\n\n                // Movement\n                this.moveSpeed = 0.15;\n                this.lookSpeed = 0.002;\n                this.keys = { w: false, a: false, s: false, d: false };\n                this.rotation = { x: 0, y: 0 };\n                this.isPointerLocked = false;\n\n                // Mobile\n                this.isMobile = /Android|iPhone|iPad|iPod|Opera Mini/i.test(navigator.userAgent);\n                this.joystickVector = new THREE.Vector2();\n                this.joystickActive = false;\n\n                // World configurations\n                this.worldConfigs = {\n                    'crystal': { \n                        emoji: '\ud83d\udc8e', \n                        color: 0x00ffff, \n                        desc: 'A world of glowing crystals and underground mysteries',\n                        gradient: ['#00ffff', '#0088ff']\n                    },\n                    'neon': { \n                        emoji: '\ud83c\udf03', \n                        color: 0xff00ff, \n                        desc: 'Cyberpunk metropolis bathed in neon lights',\n                        gradient: ['#ff00ff', '#ff006e']\n                    },\n                    'ancient': { \n                        emoji: '\ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f', \n                        color: 0xffa500, \n                        desc: 'Explore the remnants of a lost civilization',\n                        gradient: ['#ffa500', '#ff6b6b']\n                    },\n                    'ocean': { \n                        emoji: '\ud83c\udf0a', \n                        color: 0x0088ff, \n                        desc: 'An underwater realm of bioluminescent wonders',\n                        gradient: ['#0088ff', '#00ff88']\n                    },\n                    'sky': { \n                        emoji: '\u2601\ufe0f', \n                        color: 0x88ff00, \n                        desc: 'Floating islands connected by bridges of light',\n                        gradient: ['#88ff00', '#ffff00']\n                    },\n                    'forest': { \n                        emoji: '\ud83c\udf32', \n                        color: 0x00ff88, \n                        desc: 'Enchanted forest with mystical creatures',\n                        gradient: ['#00ff88', '#00ff00']\n                    },\n                    'desert': { \n                        emoji: '\ud83c\udfdc\ufe0f', \n                        color: 0xffaa00, \n                        desc: 'Vast desert with hidden oases and ancient secrets',\n                        gradient: ['#ffaa00', '#ff8800']\n                    },\n                    'space': { \n                        emoji: '\ud83d\ude80', \n                        color: 0x8844ff, \n                        desc: 'Space station orbiting unknown planets',\n                        gradient: ['#8844ff', '#ff44ff']\n                    },\n                    'volcanic': { \n                        emoji: '\ud83c\udf0b', \n                        color: 0xff4444, \n                        desc: 'Active volcanic landscape with lava flows',\n                        gradient: ['#ff4444', '#ff8844']\n                    },\n                    'arctic': { \n                        emoji: '\u2744\ufe0f', \n                        color: 0xaaeeff, \n                        desc: 'Frozen tundra with aurora borealis',\n                        gradient: ['#aaeeff', '#ffffff']\n                    }\n                };\n            }\n            \n            detectDeploymentMode() {\n                const hostname = window.location.hostname;\n                if (hostname.includes('github.io')) {\n                    return 'github-pages';\n                } else if (hostname === 'localhost' || hostname === '127.0.0.1') {\n                    return 'local';\n                } else if (window.location.protocol === 'file:') {\n                    return 'file';\n                } else {\n                    return 'web';\n                }\n            }\n\n            async init() {\n                this.setupScene();\n                this.createEnvironment();\n                await this.loadWorldData();\n                this.createWindows();\n                this.setupControls();\n                this.animate();\n\n                document.getElementById('loading').style.display = 'none';\n\n                if (this.isMobile) {\n                    document.querySelector('.controls').innerHTML = \n                        '<strong>Navigation:</strong> Touch to look \u2022 Joystick to move \u2022 Tap windows';\n                }\n            }\n\n            setupScene() {\n                // Scene with better performance settings\n                this.scene = new THREE.Scene();\n                this.scene.fog = new THREE.Fog(0x0c0c0c, 20, 80);\n\n                // Camera\n                this.camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(\n                    75, \n                    window.innerWidth / window.innerHeight, \n                    0.1, \n                    1000\n                );\n                this.camera.position.set(0, 2, 20);\n\n                // Renderer with performance optimizations\n                this.renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ \n                    antialias: false, // Disable for better performance\n                    powerPreference: \"high-performance\"\n                });\n                this.renderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);\n                this.renderer.setPixelRatio(Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio, 2));\n                this.renderer.shadowMap.enabled = false; // Disable shadows for performance\n                document.getElementById('canvas-container').appendChild(this.renderer.domElement);\n\n                // Simplified lighting\n                const ambientLight = new THREE.AmbientLight(0x404040, 1);\n                this.scene.add(ambientLight);\n\n                const dirLight = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xffffff, 0.5);\n                dirLight.position.set(10, 20, 10);\n                this.scene.add(dirLight);\n\n                // Resize handler\n                window.addEventListener('resize', () => {\n                    this.camera.aspect = window.innerWidth / window.innerHeight;\n                    this.camera.updateProjectionMatrix();\n                    this.renderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);\n                });\n            }\n\n            createEnvironment() {\n                // Simple grid for performance\n                const gridHelper = new THREE.GridHelper(80, 40, 0x0078d4, 0x1a1a1a);\n                this.scene.add(gridHelper);\n            }\n\n            async loadWorldData() {\n                try {\n                    const apiUrl = `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/${this.repoOwner}/${this.repoName}/${this.branch}/state/tree.json`;\n                    const response = await fetch(apiUrl);\n\n                    if (!response.ok) {\n                        throw new Error(`GitHub API error: ${response.status}`);\n                    }\n\n                    const data = await response.json();\n\n                    // Filter for HTML portal files\n                    this.worldData = data.tree\n                        .filter(item => \n                            item.type === 'blob' && \n                            item.path.endsWith('.html') && \n                            !item.path.includes('/') &&\n                            !item.path.toLowerCase().includes('index') &&\n                            !item.path.toLowerCase().includes('readme')\n                        )\n                        .map(item => {\n                            const name = this.formatWorldName(item.path);\n                            const config = this.getWorldConfig(item.path);\n                            \n                            // Determine the best URL based on deployment mode\n                            let url;\n                            if (this.deploymentMode === 'github-pages') {\n                                // Use GitHub Pages URL\n                                url = `https://${this.repoOwner}.github.io/${this.repoName}/${item.path}`;\n                            } else {\n                                // Use raw GitHub URL\n                                url = `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/${this.repoOwner}/${this.repoName}/${this.branch}/${item.path}`;\n                            }\n                            \n                            return {\n                                path: item.path,\n                                name: name,\n                                url: url,\n                                ...config\n                            };\n                        });\n\n                    // Update UI\n                    document.getElementById('window-count').textContent = \n                        `${this.worldData.length} worlds available`;\n\n                } catch (error) {\n                    console.error(\"Error loading worlds:\", error);\n                    // Use fallback demo data\n                    this.worldData = this.getDemoWorlds();\n                }\n            }\n\n            formatWorldName(filename) {\n                return filename\n                    .replace('.html', '')\n                    .replace(/[-_]/g, ' ')\n                    .replace(/\\b\\w/g, l => l.toUpperCase());\n            }\n\n            getWorldConfig(filename) {\n                const lower = filename.toLowerCase();\n                for (const [key, config] of Object.entries(this.worldConfigs)) {\n                    if (lower.includes(key)) {\n                        return config;\n                    }\n                }\n                // Default config\n                return {\n                    emoji: '\ud83c\udf00',\n                    color: 0x40e0d0,\n                    desc: 'A mysterious world waiting to be explored',\n                    gradient: ['#40e0d0', '#0078d4']\n                };\n            }\n\n            getDemoWorlds() {\n                return Object.entries(this.worldConfigs).map(([key, config]) => ({\n                    name: key.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + key.slice(1) + ' World',\n                    path: `${key}.html`,\n                    url: '#',\n                    ...config\n                }));\n            }\n\n            createWindows() {\n                const radius = 15;\n                const numWindows = Math.min(this.worldData.length, 10); // Limit for performance\n\n                this.worldData.slice(0, numWindows).forEach((world, index) => {\n                    const angle = (index / numWindows) * Math.PI * 2;\n                    const x = Math.cos(angle) * radius;\n                    const z = Math.sin(angle) * radius;\n                    const y = 4;\n\n                    // Window group\n                    const windowGroup = new THREE.Group();\n\n                    // Simpler window geometry for performance\n                    const frameGeometry = new THREE.BoxGeometry(4, 5, 0.2);\n                    const frameMaterial = new THREE.MeshPhongMaterial({\n                        color: world.color,\n                        emissive: world.color,\n                        emissiveIntensity: 0.2\n                    });\n                    const frame = new THREE.Mesh(frameGeometry, frameMaterial);\n\n                    // Window content plane\n                    const contentGeometry = new THREE.PlaneGeometry(3.6, 4.6);\n                    const contentMaterial = new THREE.ShaderMaterial({\n                        uniforms: {\n                            time: { value: 0 },\n                            color1: { value: new THREE.Color(world.gradient[0]) },\n                            color2: { value: new THREE.Color(world.gradient[1]) }\n                        },\n                        vertexShader: `\n                            varying vec2 vUv;\n                            void main() {\n                                vUv = uv;\n                                gl_Position = projectionMatrix * modelViewMatrix * vec4(position, 1.0);\n                            }\n                        `,\n                        fragmentShader: `\n                            uniform float time;\n                            uniform vec3 color1;\n                            uniform vec3 color2;\n                            varying vec2 vUv;\n                            \n                            void main() {\n                                vec2 center = vUv - 0.5;\n                                float dist = length(center);\n                                float wave = sin(dist * 10.0 - time * 2.0) * 0.5 + 0.5;\n                                vec3 color = mix(color1, color2, wave);\n                                float alpha = 0.8 * (1.0 - dist);\n                                gl_FragColor = vec4(color, alpha);\n                            }\n                        `,\n                        transparent: true\n                    });\n                    const content = new THREE.Mesh(contentGeometry, contentMaterial);\n                    content.position.z = 0.11;\n\n                    // Add emoji as sprite\n                    const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');\n                    canvas.width = 128;\n                    canvas.height = 128;\n                    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\n                    ctx.font = '80px Arial';\n                    ctx.textAlign = 'center';\n                    ctx.textBaseline = 'middle';\n                    ctx.fillText(world.emoji, 64, 64);\n                    \n                    const texture = new THREE.CanvasTexture(canvas);\n                    const spriteMaterial = new THREE.SpriteMaterial({ \n                        map: texture,\n                        transparent: true\n                    });\n                    const sprite = new THREE.Sprite(spriteMaterial);\n                    sprite.scale.set(2, 2, 1);\n                    sprite.position.z = 0.5;\n\n                    // Simple point light\n                    const light = new THREE.PointLight(world.color, 0.5, 10);\n                    light.position.set(x, y, z);\n                    this.scene.add(light);\n\n                    // Assemble window\n                    windowGroup.add(frame);\n                    windowGroup.add(content);\n                    windowGroup.add(sprite);\n                    windowGroup.position.set(x, y, z);\n                    windowGroup.lookAt(0, y, 0);\n\n                    // Store data\n                    content.userData = {\n                        world: world,\n                        light: light,\n                        material: contentMaterial,\n                        sprite: sprite,\n                        group: windowGroup\n                    };\n\n                    this.windows.push(content);\n                    this.scene.add(windowGroup);\n                });\n            }\n\n            setupControls() {\n                if (this.isMobile) {\n                    this.setupMobileControls();\n                } else {\n                    this.setupDesktopControls();\n                }\n            }\n\n            setupDesktopControls() {\n                // Keyboard\n                window.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {\n                    if (e.key.toLowerCase() in this.keys) {\n                        this.keys[e.key.toLowerCase()] = true;\n                    }\n                });\n\n                window.addEventListener('keyup', (e) => {\n                    if (e.key.toLowerCase() in this.keys) {\n                        this.keys[e.key.toLowerCase()] = false;\n                    }\n                });\n\n                // Mouse\n                this.renderer.domElement.addEventListener('click', () => {\n                    if (!this.isPointerLocked) {\n                        this.renderer.domElement.requestPointerLock();\n                    } else {\n                        this.checkWindowClick();\n                    }\n                });\n\n                document.addEventListener('pointerlockchange', () => {\n                    this.isPointerLocked = document.pointerLockElement === this.renderer.domElement;\n                });\n\n                document.addEventListener('mousemove', (e) => {\n                    if (this.isPointerLocked) {\n                        this.rotation.y -= e.movementX * this.lookSpeed;\n                        this.rotation.x -= e.movementY * this.lookSpeed;\n                        this.rotation.x = Math.max(-Math.PI/2, Math.min(Math.PI/2, this.rotation.x));\n                    }\n                });\n            }\n\n            setupMobileControls() {\n                const joystick = document.getElementById('joystick');\n                const handle = document.getElementById('joystick-handle');\n                let touchId = null;\n\n                // Joystick controls\n                joystick.addEventListener('touchstart', (e) => {\n                    e.preventDefault();\n                    const touch = e.touches[0];\n                    touchId = touch.identifier;\n                    this.joystickActive = true;\n                    this.updateJoystick(touch, joystick, handle);\n                });\n\n                joystick.addEventListener('touchmove', (e) => {\n                    e.preventDefault();\n                    const touch = Array.from(e.touches).find(t => t.identifier === touchId);\n                    if (touch) {\n                        this.updateJoystick(touch, joystick, handle);\n                    }\n                });\n\n                joystick.addEventListener('touchend', (e) => {\n                    e.preventDefault();\n                    this.joystickActive = false;\n                    this.joystickVector.set(0, 0);\n                    handle.style.transform = 'translate(-50%, -50%)';\n                });\n\n                // Touch look and tap\n                let lookTouch = null;\n                this.renderer.domElement.addEventListener('touchstart', (e) => {\n                    const touch = e.touches[0];\n                    lookTouch = {\n                        id: touch.identifier,\n                        x: touch.clientX,\n                        y: touch.clientY\n                    };\n\n                    // Check for window tap\n                    const rect = this.renderer.domElement.getBoundingClientRect();\n                    const x = ((touch.clientX - rect.left) / rect.width) * 2 - 1;\n                    const y = -((touch.clientY - rect.top) / rect.height) * 2 + 1;\n                    this.checkWindowClick(x, y);\n                });\n\n                this.renderer.domElement.addEventListener('touchmove', (e) => {\n                    if (!lookTouch) return;\n                    const touch = Array.from(e.touches).find(t => t.identifier === lookTouch.id);\n                    if (touch) {\n                        const deltaX = touch.clientX - lookTouch.x;\n                        const deltaY = touch.clientY - lookTouch.y;\n                        this.rotation.y -= deltaX * this.lookSpeed * 2;\n                        this.rotation.x -= deltaY * this.lookSpeed * 2;\n                        this.rotation.x = Math.max(-Math.PI/2, Math.min(Math.PI/2, this.rotation.x));\n                        lookTouch.x = touch.clientX;\n                        lookTouch.y = touch.clientY;\n                    }\n                });\n\n                this.renderer.domElement.addEventListener('touchend', () => {\n                    lookTouch = null;\n                });\n            }\n\n            updateJoystick(touch, joystick, handle) {\n                const rect = joystick.getBoundingClientRect();\n                const centerX = rect.left + rect.width / 2;\n                const centerY = rect.top + rect.height / 2;\n\n                let deltaX = touch.clientX - centerX;\n                let deltaY = touch.clientY - centerY;\n\n                const distance = Math.sqrt(deltaX * deltaX + deltaY * deltaY);\n                const maxDistance = rect.width / 2 - 25;\n\n                if (distance > maxDistance) {\n                    deltaX = (deltaX / distance) * maxDistance;\n                    deltaY = (deltaY / distance) * maxDistance;\n                }\n\n                handle.style.transform = `translate(calc(-50% + ${deltaX}px), calc(-50% + ${deltaY}px))`;\n\n                this.joystickVector.x = deltaX / maxDistance;\n                this.joystickVector.y = -deltaY / maxDistance;\n            }\n\n            checkWindowClick(mouseX = 0, mouseY = 0) {\n                this.raycaster.setFromCamera(new THREE.Vector2(mouseX, mouseY), this.camera);\n                const intersects = this.raycaster.intersectObjects(this.windows);\n\n                if (intersects.length > 0) {\n                    const window = intersects[0].object;\n                    this.enterWorld(window.userData.world);\n                }\n            }\n\n            async enterWorld(world) {\n                // Show loading\n                document.getElementById('loading').style.display = 'block';\n                document.getElementById('loading-text').textContent = `Entering ${world.name}...`;\n\n                try {\n                    // For GitHub pages deployment or direct file access\n                    const cleanUrl = world.url.replace('raw.githubusercontent.com', 'cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh')\n                                            .replace('/main/', '@main/');\n                    \n                    // First try to load directly if it's a GitHub pages URL\n                    if (world.url.includes('github.io') || world.url.includes('jsdelivr')) {\n                        window.location.href = world.url;\n                        return;\n                    }\n\n                    // For raw GitHub content, create an iframe approach\n                    const response = await fetch(world.url);\n                    const htmlContent = await response.text();\n\n                    // Create a data URL instead of blob URL to avoid security restrictions\n                    const base64 = btoa(unescape(encodeURIComponent(htmlContent)));\n                    const dataUrl = `data:text/html;base64,${base64}`;\n\n                    // Navigate to the data URL\n                    window.location.href = dataUrl;\n\n                } catch (error) {\n                    console.error('Error loading world:', error);\n                    \n                    // Fallback: try opening in new tab\n                    console.log('Attempting fallback method...');\n                    window.open(world.url, '_blank');\n                    \n                    document.getElementById('loading-text').textContent = 'Opening in new tab...';\n                    setTimeout(() => {\n                        document.getElementById('loading').style.display = 'none';\n                    }, 2000);\n                }\n            }\n\n            enterCurrentWorld() {\n                if (this.hoveredWindow) {\n                    this.enterWorld(this.hoveredWindow.userData.world);\n                }\n            }\n\n            updateMovement() {\n                const forward = new THREE.Vector3();\n                const right = new THREE.Vector3();\n\n                this.camera.getWorldDirection(forward);\n                forward.y = 0;\n                forward.normalize();\n\n                right.crossVectors(forward, new THREE.Vector3(0, 1, 0));\n\n                if (this.isMobile) {\n                    if (this.joystickActive) {\n                        const moveForward = forward.multiplyScalar(this.joystickVector.y * this.moveSpeed);\n                        const moveRight = right.multiplyScalar(this.joystickVector.x * this.moveSpeed);\n                        this.camera.position.add(moveForward);\n                        this.camera.position.add(moveRight);\n                    }\n                } else {\n                    if (this.keys.w) this.camera.position.add(forward.multiplyScalar(this.moveSpeed));\n                    if (this.keys.s) this.camera.position.add(forward.multiplyScalar(-this.moveSpeed));\n                    if (this.keys.a) this.camera.position.add(right.multiplyScalar(-this.moveSpeed));\n                    if (this.keys.d) this.camera.position.add(right.multiplyScalar(this.moveSpeed));\n                }\n\n                // Apply rotation\n                this.camera.rotation.order = 'YXZ';\n                this.camera.rotation.y = this.rotation.y;\n                this.camera.rotation.x = this.rotation.x;\n            }\n\n            updateHover() {\n                this.raycaster.setFromCamera(new THREE.Vector2(0, 0), this.camera);\n                const intersects = this.raycaster.intersectObjects(this.windows);\n\n                const info = document.getElementById('window-info');\n                if (intersects.length > 0) {\n                    const window = intersects[0].object;\n                    this.hoveredWindow = window;\n                    const world = window.userData.world;\n                    \n                    document.getElementById('window-emoji').textContent = world.emoji;\n                    document.getElementById('window-name').textContent = world.name;\n                    document.getElementById('window-desc').textContent = world.desc;\n                    document.getElementById('preview-emoji').textContent = world.emoji;\n                    \n                    // Add particles to preview\n                    this.updatePreviewParticles(world);\n                    \n                    info.classList.add('visible');\n                    \n                    // Position tooltip\n                    const vector = new THREE.Vector3();\n                    window.getWorldPosition(vector);\n                    vector.project(this.camera);\n                    const x = (vector.x * 0.5 + 0.5) * window.innerWidth;\n                    const y = (-vector.y * 0.5 + 0.5) * window.innerHeight;\n                    \n                    info.style.left = `${Math.min(x + 20, window.innerWidth - 420)}px`;\n                    info.style.top = `${Math.min(y - 50, window.innerHeight - 400)}px`;\n                } else {\n                    info.classList.remove('visible');\n                    this.hoveredWindow = null;\n                }\n            }\n\n            updatePreviewParticles(world) {\n                const container = document.getElementById('preview-particles');\n                container.innerHTML = '';\n                \n                for (let i = 0; i < 10; i++) {\n                    const particle = document.createElement('div');\n                    particle.className = 'particle';\n                    particle.style.left = Math.random() * 100 + '%';\n                    particle.style.animationDelay = Math.random() * 3 + 's';\n                    particle.style.background = world.gradient[0];\n                    container.appendChild(particle);\n                }\n            }\n\n            animate() {\n                requestAnimationFrame(() => this.animate());\n\n                const time = this.clock.getElapsedTime();\n\n                // Update movement\n                this.updateMovement();\n                this.updateHover();\n\n                // Animate windows\n                this.windows.forEach((window, index) => {\n                    // Update shader time\n                    if (window.userData.material) {\n                        window.userData.material.uniforms.time.value = time;\n                    }\n\n                    // Gentle floating\n                    window.userData.group.position.y = 4 + Math.sin(time * 0.5 + index * 0.5) * 0.2;\n                    \n                    // Rotate sprite\n                    window.userData.sprite.material.rotation = Math.sin(time + index) * 0.1;\n                    \n                    // Pulse light\n                    window.userData.light.intensity = 0.4 + Math.sin(time * 2 + index) * 0.1;\n                });\n\n                this.renderer.render(this.scene, this.camera);\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Start the app\n        const windowsNav = new WindowsNavigator();\n        windowsNav.init();\n    </script>\n</body>\n</html>", "html_sha256": "e74fd0cc85bf17c335429a5b17343b7e0450a2da1bc5c678f659e9fe31414497", "live": "https://kody-w.github.io/AINexus/windows-navigator-full.html"}, "payload_hash": "3b1fcfb6f0c37152840706a0b420871c3efb5c935ebedcc988e98fb647d81e40", "prev": null, "prev_wave": null, "sig": null, "frame_hash": "ea9465d656b362d2c0e380384802c31a39600fdc03c5e92ea146feaf613dd3ef"}
